{
  "sourceLanguage" : "en",
  "strings" : {
    "%lld photos saved and signed." : {
      "comment" : "Shown after an exposure bracket: each frame was added to the photo library as its own photo, each with a Content Credentials signature. The number is the count of photos, at least 3. Honesty wording: says only that they were saved and signed.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "A bracket never fires the flash." : {
      "comment" : "In Bracket Settings: the flash doesn't fire for any frame of an exposure bracket. Must not claim more than the English.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "A photo can't be opened or shown correctly without these. None of them identify you or link your photos." : {
      "comment" : "Explains why the locked details are always saved. Must not claim more than the English. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "%lld optional details in the files" : {
      "comment" : "Summary line in the photo details: how many of the optional details (date, camera, lens and so on) the saved files hold. The location is not counted: it has its own line. Draft wording for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "%lld optional detail in the files"
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "%lld optional details in the files"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%lld tags, blocks and properties in this file, as nope. read them back before saving it. Names are the standards' own." : {
      "comment" : "Top of a file's Every Tag page in the photo details: how many metadata items the file holds. Tag, block and property names are not translated. Keep nope. unchanged. Draft wording for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "%lld tag, block or property in this file, as nope. read it back before saving it. Names are the standards' own."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "%lld tags, blocks and properties in this file, as nope. read them back before saving it. Names are the standards' own."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A screen-size preview, not the full photo." : {
      "comment" : "Hint in the Last Photo viewer while the photo is zoomed in: what is shown is a screen-size preview held in memory, not the saved file. Honesty wording: must not claim more than the English. Draft for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "A second photo, started %@ after nope.'s, with the processing iOS applies when an app asks for the highest quality. It may combine several frames, and it may differ from what other camera apps save." : {
      "comment" : "Compare view: what the phone-processed side is. The value is a time such as 850 ms. Keep \"nope.\" unchanged. Must not claim more than the English.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "All Optional Removed" : {
      "comment" : "Settings row value: the master switch is on and no optional details are saved. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Always kept" : {
      "comment" : "In the photo details, next to a metadata item every file keeps because the photo can't be opened without it.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Always Saved" : {
      "comment" : "Section header above the details every photo keeps. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Analysis in Photos" : {
      "comment" : "Honesty heading: the Photos app analyzes photos. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "App Name and Version" : {
      "comment" : "Metadata item: records that nope. made the file. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Apple encrypts and re-signs App Store apps, so there's no standard way to confirm a download was built from our public source." : {
      "comment" : "Claim 15 in docs/research/privacy-claims.md. App Store is Apple's name. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Apple Watch Sends Only Commands" : {
      "comment" : "Honesty heading: the Apple Watch app exchanges only commands and short status with the phone. Apple Watch is Apple's product name.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "As written in the files." : {
      "comment" : "Footer of the Exposure and the Lens and Camera groups in the photo details: the values are exactly what the saved files hold. Draft wording for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Black and White Levels" : {
      "comment" : "Locked metadata item. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Camera Make and Model" : {
      "comment" : "Metadata item: which device took the photo. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Check It Yourself" : {
      "comment" : "Honesty heading: how to verify that the app makes no connections. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Claim generator: %@ %@" : {
      "comment" : "In the photo details: the software the Content Credentials manifest names as its claim generator. The values are a name and a version, such as Photivra Nope Camera 0.2.0.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Color Data and White Balance" : {
      "comment" : "Locked metadata item: color matrices and the as-shot white balance. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Color Filter Pattern" : {
      "comment" : "Locked metadata item: the sensor's red, green and blue pixel pattern. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Color Profile (HEIF and JPEG)" : {
      "comment" : "Locked metadata item. HEIF and JPEG are file format names. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Content Credentials" : {
      "comment" : "Heading in the photo details: the photo's Content Credentials signature. Content Credentials is the name of the C2PA standard's signatures. Draft wording for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Counted on the RAW sensor data when the photo was taken, over every photosite of the active area. Clipped highlights are within 0.5% of the white level or above it; clipped shadows are within 0.5% of the black level or below it, where 0.5% is of the range between the two levels." : {
      "comment" : "Footer in the photo details: how the RAW clipping is defined and measured. A photosite is one sensor element. The white and black levels are the RAW file's own values. Must not claim more than the English.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Custom" : {
      "comment" : "Settings row value: the person chose the optional details one by one. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Custom, Location On" : {
      "comment" : "Value of the Details in Each Photo row in Settings: the person chose the optional details one by one, and Location is on, so photos include where they were taken. A whole value; use the translations of Custom and Location On. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Date and Time Taken" : {
      "comment" : "Metadata item. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Details in Each Photo" : {
      "comment" : "Settings row and page title: which optional details (location, date, camera model and others) each photo includes. Replaces Choose Details and the Remove All Optional Details row. Draft wording for the Honesty review (docs/design/BUILD-SPEC.md, section 5). Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Details in each photo: Location" : {
      "comment" : "Section header above the Location switch on Details in Each Photo (its own key: Location is also the switch's name).",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Location"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Details in This Photo" : {
      "comment" : "Heading in the photo details: which metadata details the saved files hold and which they don't. Draft wording for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Developed by nope. from the RAW, Flat look" : {
      "comment" : "In the photo details, the processing of a HEIF or JPEG file: nope. developed it from the RAW with the Flat look (no contrast curve). Keep nope. unchanged.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Developed by nope. from the RAW, Standard look" : {
      "comment" : "In the photo details, the processing of a HEIF or JPEG file: nope. developed it from the RAW with the Standard look (one overall tone curve). Keep nope. unchanged.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Different" : {
      "comment" : "Heading in the compare view's details, also spoken for each item: metadata both files hold, with different values.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Distortion correction: this lens doesn't let apps turn it off or report whether it's used, so its photos may be corrected for lens distortion." : {
      "comment" : "Processing note and photo details: the lens offers no switch for the camera's geometric distortion correction, which reshapes the picture. Keep \"may\": it isn't known whether the correction is applied. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Distortion correction: this lens lets apps turn it off, and nope. does." : {
      "comment" : "Processing note and photo details: the lens lets the app turn off the camera's geometric distortion correction, which reshapes the picture. Keep \"nope.\" unchanged. Must not claim more than the English. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "DNG Version" : {
      "comment" : "Locked metadata item. DNG is a file format name. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Each frame is a separate single-frame photo. Nothing is merged." : {
      "comment" : "Explains exposure bracketing. Must not claim more than the English: the photos are never combined.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Each photo is one frame from the sensor, saved as RAW with as little processing as this phone allows. HEIF and JPEG copies are developed from it." : {
      "comment" : "Explains the format chip on the camera. RAW, HEIF and JPEG are file format names. Must not claim more than the English: as little processing as the phone allows, not zero. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Each photo is separate. Nothing is combined. Keep nope. open while the series runs." : {
      "comment" : "Explains interval shooting. Keep \"nope.\" unchanged: it is the app's name. Must not claim more than the English.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Enhanced Visual Search" : {
      "comment" : "Honesty heading. Apple's setting name: use the name iOS shows in this language. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Every camera sensor leaves a faint, unique noise pattern. With enough of your photos, forensic tools can match them to the same camera. No app can fully remove it." : {
      "comment" : "Claim 9 in docs/research/privacy-claims.md (peer-reviewed). Must not claim more than the English. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Every tag, block and property nope. read back from each file before saving it, with its value." : {
      "comment" : "Footer of Every Tag in the photo details. Keep nope. unchanged. Draft wording for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Exact Model for RAW Editors" : {
      "comment" : "Metadata item: the exact device model, used by RAW editing apps to pick a color profile. RAW is a file format name. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Exposure Settings" : {
      "comment" : "Metadata item: shutter speed, ISO, aperture and focal length. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Exposure Settings is off, so the files don't hold the exposure. These are the values the camera reported for this photo. nope. keeps them only until it closes." : {
      "comment" : "Footer of the Exposure group in the photo details when the files hold no exposure: the shutter and ISO shown are what the camera reported, kept in memory until the app closes. Exposure Settings is the name of the setting. Keep nope. unchanged. Draft wording for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Faces and Autofocus" : {
      "comment" : "Honesty heading: iOS may detect faces to choose where to focus.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Fixed values the file standard asks for, such as version numbers and the color space. Nothing in them identifies you or your phone." : {
      "comment" : "Explains the Standard File Tags switch. No default note. Must not claim more than the English. Draft wording for the Honesty review (docs/design/BUILD-SPEC.md, section 5). Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "HEIF with some device processing" : {
      "comment" : "Spoken format name for the no-RAW fallback. HEIF is a file format name.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Hold the time since the device restarted and IDs for each photo, which can link your photos. Off: nothing visible changes." : {
      "comment" : "What maker notes contain, and what turning them off costs. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Honesty" : {
      "comment" : "Settings row and screen title: what nope. does and doesn't do, and what it can't control. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "iCloud Photos" : {
      "comment" : "Honesty heading. Apple's feature name: use the name iOS shows in this language. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "If you opt in, Apple may share aggregated, non-identifying crash and usage statistics with developers. They never include your photos. It's in Settings › Privacy & Security › Analytics & Improvements." : {
      "comment" : "Claim 12 and note 12 in docs/research/privacy-claims.md. Use the setting names iOS shows in this language. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Image Size and Layout" : {
      "comment" : "Locked metadata item: image size, bit depth, compression and data layout. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "In Night Mode, shows the live picture in red too. Only the screen changes; photos keep their colors." : {
      "comment" : "Explains the Red Viewfinder switch, which is always shown and takes effect in night mode. Night Mode is the name of nope.'s switch; use its translation. Must not claim more than the English. Draft wording for the Honesty review (docs/design/BUILD-SPEC.md, section 5). Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "In Photos" : {
      "comment" : "Row in the photo details: how the files were added to the Photos app. Photos is the system photo library app. Draft wording for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "In the files" : {
      "comment" : "In the photo details: the saved files hold this detail. Draft wording for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "iOS Connections" : {
      "comment" : "Honesty heading: iOS itself goes online. iOS is a product name. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "iOS itself, for example iCloud Photos, makes its own connections." : {
      "comment" : "Claim 1 in docs/research/privacy-claims.md. iOS and iCloud Photos are Apple's names. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "iOS may detect faces in the viewfinder to decide where to focus. Focus on Faces in nope.'s settings decides only whether nope.'s autofocus and auto exposure follow them. nope. doesn't read or save which faces it found." : {
      "comment" : "Honesty statement under Faces and Autofocus. Claim 18 in docs/research/privacy-claims.md (AVCaptureDevice face-driven autofocus and auto exposure); issue #80. Focus on Faces is the name of nope.'s own switch; use its translation. Must not say that the switch turns face detection off. Must not claim more than the English. Keep \"nope.\" unchanged. Draft wording for the Honesty review (docs/design/BUILD-SPEC.md, section 5). Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "iOS Version" : {
      "comment" : "Metadata item: the operating system version. iOS is a product name; keep it unchanged. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "JPEG with some device processing" : {
      "comment" : "Spoken format name for the no-RAW fallback. JPEG is a file format name.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Keep Screen On" : {
      "comment" : "Honesty heading: what the Keep Screen On switch does to the screen, the battery and locking. Keep Screen On is the name of nope.'s own switch; use its translation. Draft wording for the Honesty review (issue #97). Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Keep Screen On stops the screen from locking by itself while the camera is showing, so the camera keeps running and uses more battery. The screen dims to 10% after 2 minutes without a touch (30 seconds in Low Power Mode). After 30 minutes without a touch or a photo, the phone's Auto-Lock applies again. While the screen is on, the phone is unlocked. The side button always locks it." : {
      "comment" : "Issue #97; docs/design/keep-screen-on.md, wording 7. Keep Screen On is the name of nope.'s own switch; Low Power Mode and Auto-Lock are Apple's names: use the names iOS shows in this language. Must not claim more than the English. Draft wording for the Honesty review. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Kept by nope. until it closes, to group the frames here. Not written to the files; in Photos each frame is a separate photo." : {
      "comment" : "Footer of the Bracket group in the photo details. Keep \"nope.\" unchanged: it is the app's name. Must not claim more than the English: the values are in memory only.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Latitude, longitude and altitude, while the camera is open. Off: nothing is lost." : {
      "comment" : "What the Location item writes into each photo, and what turning it off costs. Must not claim more than the English.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Left Out" : {
      "comment" : "Disclosure row in the photo details: the optional details the saved files don't hold, each with the reason. Draft wording for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Lens and camera names are off in Settings, so the files don't hold them." : {
      "comment" : "Footer of the Lens and Camera group in the photo details when the files hold no lens or camera names: the lens shown is the one that was selected. Draft wording for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Lens Correction Instructions" : {
      "comment" : "Metadata item: instructions editors can use to correct lens distortion. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Lens Make and Model" : {
      "comment" : "Metadata item: which lens took the photo. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Lenses Without RAW" : {
      "comment" : "Honesty heading: on a lens that can't save RAW, the phone processes the photo. RAW is a file format name. Draft wording for the Honesty review (docs/design/BUILD-SPEC.md, section 5). Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Lets anyone check that the photo hasn't changed since nope. saved it. A signed photo shows that it was taken with nope., and which version." : {
      "comment" : "Explains the Sign Each Photo switch. No default note. Must not claim more than the English: the signature shows changes, it doesn't prove who took the photo; it names the app and its version. Keep \"nope.\" unchanged. Draft wording for the Honesty review (docs/design/BUILD-SPEC.md, section 5). Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Live aids are measured on the preview, a few times a second, only while they show. Nothing is saved." : {
      "comment" : "Note under the focus peaking, histogram and live readout switches. Must not claim more than the English.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Location" : {
      "comment" : "Metadata item: where the photo was taken. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Location access is off for nope., so photos can't include a location. To add one, allow location access in Settings." : {
      "comment" : "Shown under the Location switch when the person declined location access. Keep \"nope.\" unchanged. Must not claim more than the English.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Location access isn't allowed on this device, so photos can't include a location." : {
      "comment" : "Shown under the Location switch when a restriction, such as Screen Time, doesn't allow location access. Must not claim more than the English.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Location is in the files" : {
      "comment" : "Summary line in the photo details: the saved files hold the location where the photo was taken (GPS). Shown with a warning symbol. Draft wording for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Location is off unless you turn it on under Details in Each Photo in nope.'s settings. Then nope. uses your location only while the camera is open, and each photo gets its latitude, longitude and altitude. No direction, speed or GPS time is written, and the location is never sent anywhere." : {
      "comment" : "Issue #43; docs/PRIVACY.md, \"Location\". Honesty statement under Location Only If You Turn It On. Details in Each Photo is the name of nope.'s own settings page; use its translation. Keep \"nope.\" unchanged. Must not claim more than the English. Draft wording for the Honesty review (docs/design/BUILD-SPEC.md, section 5). Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Location is on, but location access is off, so photos are saved without a location." : {
      "comment" : "Explanation of the Location On chip when the person turned Location on but location access is off in the system settings. Must not claim more than the English.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Location On" : {
      "comment" : "Warning chip on the camera: new photos include where they were taken.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Location Only If You Turn It On" : {
      "comment" : "Honesty heading: photos include a location only when the person turns Location on.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Location stays off, because location access isn't allowed for nope. You can allow it in Settings." : {
      "comment" : "Shown after applying a settings preset that includes Location when location access is off. Keep \"nope.\" unchanged. Must not claim more than the English.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Locked" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver: this detail is always saved and can't be turned off. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
